Q1, which joins all of player 1’s activity rows, will sum two day‑1 events (giving a numerator of 2 while the denominator is COUNT(DISTINCT) = 1, resulting in a retention of 2.00), whereas Q2 will produce a single match from its LEFT JOIN (yielding a retention of 1.00).
