  Total = 3, and the denominator is the count of players (3), so Q1 returns 3/3 = 1.00.

• Q2, on the other hand, uses a window function so that for each player only the first login’s gap is considered. It will count player 1 and player 2 once each (since each has a next-day login for their first event) and not count player 3. Thus the numerator is 2 (distinct players), the denominator is 3, and Q2 returns 2/3 = 0.67.

This counterexample shows that if duplicate next‐day logins are present, the two queries are not equivalent.
