-- the set of followers is { 'Bob', 'Charlie', 'Alice', 'Dave' } and the intersection with the set
-- of followees gives { 'Alice', 'Bob' } only. Both queries then group on these values and return identical counts.

-- Because of the schema constraints (no nulls, no duplicate rows), it is impossible to generate a
-- counterexample where Q1 and Q2 produce different results.

