INSERT INTO ACTIVITY (PLAYER_ID, EVENT_DATE, DEVICE_ID, GAMES_PLAYED) VALUES (2, '2023-01-02', 201, 6);

/*
Running Q1 on this data will join the MIN_DATE from the subquery with all activities for each player. For PLAYER 1, both rows on 2023-01-02
satisfy the condition (MIN_DATE + 1 = '2023-01-02'), so they contribute a total of 2 to the SUM. For PLAYER 2, there is one matching row. Thus
Q1 computes the numerator as 3 and divides by 2 (the number of players), yielding 1.50 (after rounding to 2 decimals).

Q2, however, looks only at each player’s first row (the earliest activity). For both players the first activity is on 2023-01-01, and the
immediate next activity is 2023-01-02. Thus each player is counted only once (the numerator is 2), so Q2 returns 1.00.

This difference shows that the two queries are not equivalent when there are duplicate consecutive-day activities for a player.
*/

