/*
Assume for the sake of this counterexample that due to a data‐quality issue the primary key constraint is not enforced and duplicate events for a given player on the same day can exist. 

We insert two players. For player 1 the install date is 2021-01-01 and there are two separate records on 2021-01-02 (the day after install). For player 2 the install date is 2021-01-01 and there is one record on 2021-01-02.
When grouping by install date, Q1 will use the join to get three rows qualifying for day+1 out of two distinct players (thus summing 2 + 1 = 3 in the numerator, even though player 1 should only contribute 1), while Q2 will pick only one next event per player, yielding a numerator of 1 + 1 = 2. This causes the DAY1_RETENTION values to diverge.
*/

