/*
Assuming a version of the schema where duplicate sessions on the same day are allowed (i.e. ignoring the PRIMARY KEY on (PLAYER_ID, EVENT_DATE) for this example), the following inserts produce a difference in output between Q1 and Q2.

In this test data:
 • Player 1 installs on 2020-01-01 and then has two activity records on 2020-01-02 (day after install).
   Q1 will add 1 for each day-1 record and get a numerator of 2 for player 1, whereas Q2 will count player 1 only once.
 • Player 2 installs on 2020-01-01 but has no activity on 2020-01-02.
Thus, when grouping by the install date 2020-01-01, Q1 computes:
    INSTALLS = 2 and DAY1_RETENTION = (2 (from player1) + 0 (from player2)) / 2 = 1.00
while Q2 computes:
    INSTALLS = 2 and DAY1_RETENTION = (1 (from player1) + 0) / 2 = 0.50
*/

